## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/services/submit-reservations/apply-report-discounts.service.ts** (`applyReportDiscountsService`): This is where report.price.discount (the promo amount sent to Mozio) is computed/assigned. The match at lines 15-19, `dispatch.lineItems.some((lineItem) => lineItem.id === discount.lineItemId)`, compares a dispatch line-item key against a raw order line-item id. For return trips, mapOrderDispatchesToMozioDispatches (submit-reservations.mappers.ts:184) rewrites the dispatch line-item id via getDispatchLineItemKey(id, true) to `<id>#return`, while getUniqDiscounts sets discount.lineItemId to the bare lineItem.id. So for return-trip dispatches the ids never match, discountsForDispatch is empty, the function returns early, and no discount amount is ever written to dispatch.report.price.discount — hence the promo amount missing for Return trip tickets.
  - **Minimal fix:** In applyReportDiscountsService, change the filter predicate at lines 16-18 from `dispatch.lineItems.some((lineItem) => lineItem.id === discount.lineItemId)` to `dispatch.lineItems.some((lineItem) => parseDispatchLineItemKey(lineItem.id).id === discount.lineItemId)` so the composite `<id>#return` dispatch key is parsed back to the bare order line-item id before comparison. Reuse the EXISTING helper parseDispatchLineItemKey (defined in src/services/helpers/order/dispatch-line-item-key.ts) by adding `import { parseDispatchLineItemKey } from '~/services/helpers/order';` — the same import path already used for getDispatchLineItemKey in submit-reservations.mappers.ts:4. No new logic needed; one-expression change plus one import.


